{
  "description": "A family-aware diagnostic adapter for Self-EvolveRec that measures the behavior of the actual trained NextItNet model and generates an interpretation prompt grounded in measured metrics and their definitions.",
  "motivation": "Support model improvement using reproducible diagnostics while preserving the NextItNet backbone, benchmark protocol, available-data constraints, and one independently trained model per category.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Preserve ModelView compatibility through view.model, item_emb, log2feats(sequence), predict_score(features, items), user_train, meta_data, and review_data. Batches contain (None, sequence, positive, negative), with tensors shaped B × L. Adapt probes to NextItNet’s causal convolutional representations and use the final nonpadding position for left-padded histories. Report only measurements supported by public histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps; treat unavailable review fields and simulator traits as unobserved. Keep checkpoints and generated predictors consistent. Route four categories to their respective single models. Use the host’s macro-average validation HR@10 for selection; diagnostics do not replace that evaluator.",
  "pseudocode": "Initialize DiagnosisProbe(view, device)\nFor each diagnostic batch:\n    Unpack (_, sequence, positive, negative)\n    Compute NextItNet features through view.log2feats(sequence)\n    Exclude padding from applicable measurements\n    Use the final nonpadding position when a sequence-level feature is needed\n    Compute supported diagnostics through the actual model and compatibility interfaces\nAggregate measurements with explicit definitions and valid-sample counts\nReturn {metrics, metric_definitions}\nBuild diagnosis_interpreter_prompt from returned measurements and definitions\nGenerate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for five real training users per category\nSelect model changes using the host's four-category macro validation HR@10",
  "originality": {
    "score": 4,
    "positive": "Connects architecture-aware diagnostics with explicit data provenance and a fixed evaluation contract.",
    "negative": "The supplied description specifies an integration interface rather than a novel diagnostic algorithm."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Can support systematic diagnosis and targeted improvements as the single NextItNet architecture evolves.",
    "negative": "Its usefulness depends on choosing reliable diagnostic measurements; the description does not specify concrete metrics or demonstrate predictive value."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "The required interfaces and batch structure provide clear implementation boundaries.",
    "negative": "Correct padding handling, architecture-specific probes, missing-data handling, and checkpoint/predictor consistency require careful integration."
  }
}
